# io_uring, and who may ask the kernel for one.
#
# 0 lets every process create io_uring instances, which is the kernel's own
# default.  1 refuses unprivileged processes outside the group below.  2 refuses
# everybody, CAP_SYS_ADMIN included.
#
# The group only bites at 1.  At 0 and 2 it is inert, and is written anyway so
# that changing the mode is a one-line edit rather than a two-line one.
#
# %IO_URING_GID% is filled in by the makefile fragment: a group's gid is only
# knowable on the guest, and this setting takes the number rather than the name.
kernel.io_uring_disabled = [% mode %]
kernel.io_uring_group = %IO_URING_GID%
